<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition IV.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming that Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption III.1. ‣ III Preliminaries ‣ Understanding the Role of Rehearsal Scale in Continual Learning under Varying Model Capacities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption III.3. ‣ III Preliminaries ‣ Understanding the Role of Rehearsal Scale in Continual Learning under Varying Model Capacities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III.3</span></a> hold. For <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the generalization error <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{G}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{w}}_{T})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{G}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{w}}_{T})]</annotation></semantics></math> increases with error on initial task when <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\boldsymbol{w}_{2}^{*}-\boldsymbol{w}_{1}^{*}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\boldsymbol{w}_{2}^{*}-\boldsymbol{w}_{1}^{*}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> is low. Minimizing error requires small memory and adaptation errors while maintaining performance on the initial task.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is provided in Appendix D. As indicated by Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition IV.5. ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Understanding the Role of Rehearsal Scale in Continual Learning under Varying Model Capacities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.5</span></a>, better generalization requires excelling at current task while retaining knowledge from previous tasks. In addition, performance on initial task is also crucial, consistent with the empirical analyses by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. From the perspective of memorability, failing to learn initial task well can lead to error accumulation if knowledge retention is overemphasized.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Empirical Validation on DNNs</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus far, we have explored different aspects influencing the performance of rehearsal-based continual learning. To validate whether these theoretical insights under overparameterization extend to deep neural networks, we conduct experiments on standard real-world datasets. After training each task, the adaptation, memory, and generalization errors were systematically evaluated. The experiments were conducted on MNIST <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> , CIFAR-10 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite> , CIFAR-100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite>, and Tiny-ImageNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>. All experiments were repeated at least three times, and average results are reported, with details provided in Appendix H.</p>
</div>
